  "body": "**What happened:** PR #1044 (#1015) changed the 5-axis stamp shank refusal in `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/` so that it carries a ghost (`CommandError::MachiningGhost`). Its author's `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` came out green, but never ran `crates/app/tests/operations.rs`, where `multiaxis_rough_refuses_a_slot_the_cone_cannot_clear` pins that refusal through `GenerateOperation`. That test failed. The failure surfaced only when a stacked merge made quick run the whole app suite list, and it was fixed on the PR.\n\n**Why:** `operations.rs`'s Gate map names app modules only, so a change to `motion::multiaxis` (or other motion generators that `operations.rs` exercises end to end) doesn't select it. The same class of gap as #922 / #1021: a change can pass quick while the suite that pins its behaviour sits out.\n\n**Done means:** `operations.rs`'s Gate map names the motion modules its tests pin (at least `motion::multiaxis`, and the generators it drives end to end), checked against its test list; an xtask unit test pins that a change under `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/` selects `operations`. Coordinate with #965 / #1021 (same header lines).\n",
